note: three-tab finance diagnostic (Summary, Drivers, Outlook) on the reference report design system (dark-grey banner #1F242F with a lime #EEFB87 rule, Messina Sans / Calibri with monospace uppercase labels, dark table headers with banded rows, 0.75px hairlines, square corners, favourable #3BA184, unfavourable fills #BF9856 with negative figures in #B23A3A, light and dark themes), insight-led: a 3-5 bullet executive summary where every bullet is an observation followed by what it means (net-income lead, admitted reviewed conclusions when present, engine insights on persistence, concentration, margin trend, mix and budget bias, then the full-year implication), a P&L strip in order of calculation, charts first, text only in the drill-down drawers, and a collapsible, tab-aware glossary at the foot (the open tab's labels first plus the shared groups, or every label on the page). Negatives print in brackets; engine prose is softened ("adverse" -> "unfavourable", "mm" -> "mn"). The renderer computes nothing economic; it reads the payload and the admitted diagnosis and formats them. Allowed render-stage arithmetic: chart geometry, display sign flips, sums of engine-emitted facts for a dimension lens, shares for display.
1.4.1: the Window and Compare toggles stay on the right of the title at desktop width (they wrap below only under 980px).
1.4.1: Compare lists vs Prior year first, and the page opens on Month vs Prior year by default (analyze_finance.py --basis budget to open on budget).
1.5.0: only the summary roll-up keys in config/scope.json are dropped; an unknown negative key refuses the build.
1.5.0: subsidiary exclusions (config/scope.json exclude_subsidiaries, --exclude-subsidiary, --no-default-exclusions); the header, source line and meta.scope.label read 'All subsidiaries (N) excluding ...'.
1.5.0: governed reconciliation: the extract must tie to REVENUE_MTD, ADJUSTED_EBITDA_MTD and NET_INCOME_MTD within $1 for every month and subsidiary in scope (--governed, required with --rows), or the build refuses naming them.
1.5.0: account identity is account number + name within subsidiary (CHART_OF_ACCOUNT_KEY is account x class); class and department are drill detail; an account whose budget is held on another entity is compared across subsidiaries.
1.5.0: every account and driver carries movement and movement_basis (both / no_comparator / no_activity); rankings, shares, concentration, 'Mostly ...' sentences and bridge steps use movement; one-sided rows show a 'New this period' or 'Not this period' chip.
1.5.0: lenses[*].reconciliation: per driver, the accounts (top N, remainder, total = driver movement) and the Department > Account split, validated to the cent; the drawer shows the reconciling table and a comparator-to-actual mini waterfall.
1.5.0: lenses[*].splits: per account, the subsidiary, class and department split; where the comparator is not held at that level the rows show actuals and 'No budget at this level', never a member variance.
1.5.0: executive summary bullets are built by the engine (lenses[*].summary) with registered figures, a claim the validator re-checks against the numbers, and a drill target the bullet opens (section > L4 drivers > accounts).
1.5.0: decisions for management: one fact-built question per material driver (movement, department, lead account with subsidiary, one-sided / recurring / one-off) in actions[*].ask.
1.5.0: month labels from the period start date (Sep '25), on every chart; Plan vs month plots drivers (top ten, the rest grouped) with paired Plan / Month / No budget line segments.
1.5.0: ?selftest page hook for the headless test: label overlaps, month-label format, Plan vs month row count and the lead bullet's drill.
1.5.1: selecting a bar in the Adjusted EBITDA bridge (or a driver in the By subsidiary list) re-targets the selected-driver panel, the usual-range panel and the By subsidiary bars together.
1.5.1: drill tables leave out rows with no movement and say how many ("N accounts with no movement in this view are not shown"): account, department, class and subsidiary tables, the action drawer's accounts and the subsidiary bars; engine tables carry zero_count and still foot.
1.5.1: splits against prior year (and account rows) always show movement, new and stopped accounts included; only a budget held at a coarser grain shows actuals with "No budget at this level".
1.5.1: every element that opens a drill shows a pointer cursor; drill tables wrap long names and chips inside their panel.
1.5.1: plain-language labels: Data verified / From the data / Test data and AI reviewed / Not yet AI reviewed replace engine baseline and admitted diagnosis; the banner, data badge, footer, glossary, decisions, data-checks drawer (named checks; OK / Note / Failed / Not run), statement labels (What the data shows / What it suggests / Possible explanation) and pattern labels read in plain words; engine prose shown on the page maps comparator, mechanical and run-rate reference to everyday terms; the headless test refuses technical wording on the page.
1.5.1: By subsidiary reads the engine's split (reconciliation[*].by_subsidiary per driver, lenses[*].by_subsidiary for all accounts): variance bars against prior year, and against budget only where the budget is held by subsidiary; otherwise actuals with a note, so a budget held on one entity no longer shows each subsidiary's revenue as a variance. With no bridge bar selected the side panels show All accounts (listed first); choosing All accounts clears the bar selection.
1.6.0 (contract 1.3.0): the Summary lead for a result carried below the line names the item that carries it (for example "Ahead, mostly on Income Taxes") and says whether operations moved the same way, the other way or held; a department is named in a decision ask or driver reading only when the driver spans at least two departments that each carry 5% or more of the gross movement.
1.6.0: Drivers tab: Plan vs month removed (the engine still computes the layers for the actions); the usual-range and By subsidiary panels sit under the bridge; By subsidiary is shown against prior year only; the selected driver's By account and By department blocks start collapsed with a count and total; every "N other accounts / departments" row expands to its members (contract 1.3.0: reconciliation[*].other.items and split other.items, validated to foot).
1.6.0: Outlook tab: a run-rate rule picker (also by clicking a rule's bar) drives the tiles, the monthly chart, the full-year bridge and the run-rate drawer; an info button explains run-rate and the rule in use with its months and figures (contract 1.3.0: each sensitivity rule carries path, months_used, how, remaining_value, remaining_effect, gap_vs_budget and gap_vs_prior_year, with the identity checked per rule). The Summary tab keeps the trailing three-month average.
1.6.0: If current gaps continue: a category list and favourable / unfavourable bars of each driver's remaining months at the picked run-rate rule against its remaining budget (outlook.gap_view); the operating categories add up to the full-year bridge's remaining step, so the panel, bridge and tiles move together when the rule changes. The run-rate drawer adds a vs budget column and its rule bars switch the rule.
1.6.0: every chart line is solid except the run-rate projection of the remaining months (dotted); the persistence tag reads "One-off" (was "One-off?").
1.7.0 (contract 1.4.0): size thresholds scale with the window (2.5% / 1.25% / 0.35% of an average month's revenue times the months in the window; the month's large threshold is about $190k on the Sep-26 data, was $460k for every window); each lens carries its own materiality; a sign flip (a credit became an expense) carries no percentage and takes the dollar test alone.
1.7.0: the engine's own prose passes the diagnosis gate's wording lint (no causal wording, no forbidden phrases): "driven by demand" and "short-term squeeze" reworded; validate.py refuses engine text that fails it.
1.7.0: window tie-out: the view's QTD / YTD / LTM columns at the as-of month against the extract's window sums, by subsidiary and consolidated (within 0.1% or $5k passes, within 1% is a note, beyond 1% fails), as the window_tie_out data check with its differences in the data-checks drawer; the governed query carries the window columns.
1.7.0: one-off register per window (an unusual month outside the trailing range by a significant amount, or a single posting on an account with no history, at the management threshold; offsetting pairs marked); an item at a quarter or more of the net-income movement and at least the large threshold is named in the lead with net income without it; the run-rate outlook replaces the flagged months by the account's trend reference, and the run-rate drawer lists them.
1.7.0: the Month and Year-to-date views on the page's basis need an admitted AI review before the page is published (--diagnosis takes one file per view; --allow-missing-review publishes with a visible notice); the banner names the reviewed and missing views; the footer reads "this view not AI reviewed" per view.
1.7.0: data age in the header (days after the period end, noted beyond 30 days, was 45); target dates are the build date plus ten business days (were period end plus 30 days).
1.7.0: an Assumptions dropdown under "How to read this page": every threshold, test and rule in use for every window, from meta.assumptions (the engine formats it; the page computes nothing).
1.8.0 (diagnosis contract 1.1.0): the executive summary and the decisions for management are written by the reviewer, not filled from templates. The admitted review carries cfo.summary: 3 to 5 bullets (a bold lead of at most eight words, then at most 45 words: observation with registered figures, then what it means; net income first; each with a drill that opens on its evidence and a tone) and 2 or 3 decisions (questions, a suggested owner, a drill, an optional registered amount at stake). The gate refuses a figure alone, an unregistered figure, a drill that does not exist, causal wording, a decision that is not a question, or a lead not about net income. finance_brief.py summary_pack lists every figure the writer may use with its source and the rules. The engine's own bullets remain the fallback where no review is admitted for the view.
1.8.1 (diagnosis contract 1.2.0): every executive-summary bullet is one short line on the page (the bold lead plus at most 15 words, no figures or account numbers); clicking it opens the full sentence with its registered figures above the evidence it drills to. The engine adds `short` to each of its bullets; a written bullet carries `text` (the line) and `detail` (the full sentence), and the gate refuses a line over 15 words or with a figure, or a detail over 60 words. The Adjusted EBITDA drawer lists the operating drivers (revenue, cost of sales, operating expenses) instead of "Nothing moved".
1.8.2: the data-age note is no longer in the header or the banner; it stays in the data checks (How recent the data is, noted beyond 30 days) and in the Assumptions list.
1.9.0 (contract 1.5.0): the view's COA_MAPPING_L5 / L6 under each driver: the By sub-group drill (L4 › L5 › L6 › account) in the driver panel and drawer, a level that repeats its parent collapsed, each level footing to the one above (invariant I13, QC l5_footing / l6_footing, fail closed); Revenue by product line on the Drivers tab with a Month / window toggle; Operating expenses by sub-group (S&M, R&D, G&A at L5 / L6); the node: drawer. The page still computes nothing economic: every figure is in lenses[].hierarchy and lenses[].product_lines.
1.9.1: the Revenue by product line and Operating expenses by sub-group panels are off the Drivers tab (sub-groups stay in each driver's By sub-group drill); the driver drawer's account waterfall shows the top three accounts plus Other, keyed 1, 2, 3, Other on the axis, with names, amounts and colours in a key below the chart.
1.9.2: the AI reviewed badge is removed from the section headers, detail panels, executive-summary bullets, the data badge, the footer and the glossary; the banner still says which views were reviewed.
1.9.3: fix: the Outlook tab (and the Drivers review section) rendered blank on the reviewed view, the page's opening view, because the review headings still called diagMark(), the badge helper retired in 1.9.2; it is restored as a no-op. Switching to an unreviewed view had hidden the error. The test review now carries a structural conclusion and a forecast assumption, so both sections render in the headless check.
1.10.0: Drivers tab: the Adjusted EBITDA bridge's axis labels are tilted 45 degrees so long category names never overlap; 3-5 drillable commentary bullets sit beside the bridge and follow By driver / To net income and the Window and Compare toggles (result, largest unfavourable and favourable drivers with their lead account, split by line, concentration and persistence); layout is bridge | commentary, usual range | selected category, By subsidiary | selected category (continued), then How to read this page and Assumptions.
1.10.0: Outlook tab: 3-5 drillable bullets under Where the year lands follow the run-rate rule picked (landing vs budget and last year, banked year to date, drivers ahead of and behind the remaining budget, rule spread and recurring gaps); the KPI tiles follow; Monthly Adjusted EBITDA | How much the rule matters and Full-year bridge | If current gaps continue sit side by side at equal width. The commentary selects and phrases engine fields only.
1.10.1: commentary names open their drill without a dotted underline (underline on hover only); the admitted AI review sits inside the summary panel it belongs to (Drivers: what is lasting, under the bridge commentary; Outlook: forecast assumptions, under Where the year lands) instead of a section at the foot; the Outlook KPIs stand in a highlighted column beside the summary (full-year run-rate first, larger figures, a dark left rule), wrapping to two by two under 900px.
1.10.2: the review block is headed "What this means" and shows on every view: on Drivers the admitted structural reading where the view is reviewed, otherwise the engine's fired pattern readings for that window and comparison; on Outlook the reviewed forecast assumptions whatever the view (the projection is one fiscal-year figure), or the engine's projection caveat when no view is reviewed.
1.10.3: a driver's share of movement is taken within the bridge it sits on (drivers[].share_scope: ebitda for revenue, cost of sales and opex; below_ebitda for synergies and non-operating items), so the Adjusted EBITDA bridge's bars add up to 100% and the steps to net income add up to 100% on their own (was a share of every P&L driver, so the EBITDA bars summed well short of 100%). The driver tile reads "Share of EBITDA movement" (or "Share of below-EBITDA movement"); the Concentrated bullet, the driver drawer, the engine's driver statements and the summary concentration bullet say "of the Adjusted EBITDA movement"; validate.py refuses driver shares that do not add up to 100% within a bridge. Account shares are unchanged (share of all accounts' movement).
1.10.4: a sign and colour legend ("Favourable and unfavourable", `signLegend`) sits open above How to read this page on every tab, no drop-down, as a table (Outcome, Figure, Bar, Colour and sign, Meaning; the Colour and sign column drops under 720px): favourable is green with a plus sign (helps profit: more revenue or less cost); unfavourable is a red figure in brackets with a gold bar (hurts profit: less revenue or more cost); in line is grey (smaller than the smallest move reported); brackets in black are a negative amount, not a judgement.
1.10.5: EBITDA (and S&M, G&A, R&D, COGs) keep their capitals wherever a label is lower-cased inside a sentence or title: the page's lc() and the engine's common.lower_words() lower only words written as one capital plus lower-case letters (the section drawer read "Adjusted ebitda"; engine sentences read "adjusted ebitda" and "fully loaded s&m expense"). The test opens the EBITDA drawers and refuses lower-case ebitda on the page or in any engine sentence.
1.10.6: the variance legend (was 'Favourable and unfavourable') is headed 'Variance legend: how favourable and unfavourable moves are shown', in smaller type, with four columns: Outcome, Bar, Text colour and sign (the text itself in that colour, with an example figure: green with a plus sign, red in brackets, grey either sign, black in brackets) and Meaning; the separate Figure column is gone.
